# Design the task before styling the screen

- Identify the operator, current branch, primary action, frequency, and device from the request and nearby workflow. Read only relevant product constraints.
- Base decisions on usability, existing identity, and evidence appropriate to the task. DESIGN.md may provide context when relevant. Choose improvements using design judgment.
- Reuse established good patterns. For a genuinely new workflow or major redesign, use karman-ux-benchmark to answer one concrete design question, then karman-ui-design for the chosen direction. Load only the relevant skill.
- A local field or visual fix normally needs the existing component and applicable framework docs. Reuse a previously established benchmark decision.
- Choose one direction, implement it, and briefly explain the meaningful tradeoff. Resolve ordinary font, spacing, hierarchy, and interaction choices autonomously within the task.

## Review the touched journey

| Area | Check before handoff |
| --- | --- |
| Hierarchy | Clear primary action, readable density, related information together, current branch and record visible. |
| Fields | Suitable input type, formatting, labels, sensible defaults, validation timing, recoverable values. |
| Feedback | Targeted loading, accurate success/failure, understandable disabled states, stale results handled. |
| Lists | Distinguish no data from no matches, useful filter reset, bounded results, stable sorting and pagination. |
| Keyboard | Tab order, Enter behavior, visible focus, dialog focus return, scanner speed when relevant. |
| Arabic/English | Joined Arabic letters, long labels, logical spacing, isolated identifiers and amounts, translated errors. |
| Responsive | Main task usable at the intended desktop/tablet width, appropriate touch targets, controlled overflow. |
| Recovery | Preserve work, explain the next safe action, distinguish pending from completed, respect frozen payments. |
| Accessibility | Semantics, labels, error association, contrast, keyboard operation, readable status text. |

Apply the rows relevant to the change during implementation and self-review. A small fix does not require a whole-site audit.

## Finish with evidence appropriate to risk

- The verification policy in 000-core.mdc governs ownership and scope.
- Omar performs routine rendered UI and print walkthroughs. Supply up to three concrete checks.
- Invoke karman-ui-review for a requested visual review or a browser-specific defect. Select only the viewport, role, and boundary needed to establish that behavior.
- Describe unperformed browser checks as pending. A screenshot or successful render alone does not establish the action's behavior.
